meta {
  name: Delete Pipeline
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/pipelines/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~confirmedRemovalIds: 
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
  id: {{pipelineId}}
}

tests {
  test("Status code is 204", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(204);
  });
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` and `pipelineId` are set. The DataSet is in `DRAFT`.

  Each DataSink that loses its last Pipeline with this delete becomes inactive: a never provisioned one is deleted, a provisioned one is marked `PENDING_UNPROVISION` until the next release removes its storage. Its Layers are deleted. An API of the DataSet goes, together with its Layers, when no active DataSink of a kind that backs it remains: PostGIS for OWS, FROST for STA. All of this happens in one transaction.

  **Confirmation:** When the delete removes a provisioned DataSink, a Layer or an API, the request must name each of them in `confirmedRemovalIds` (repeatable UUID query parameter). Get the ids from `datasets/get-removal-impact` with `deletedPipelineIds`, or from the `impact` of a `409`. Without them the backend answers `409` with type `urn:civitas:error:REMOVAL_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED` and changes nothing. The Pipeline of this collection has no DataSink at this point, so it goes without confirmation; `dataset-saga-workflow` steps 14c to 15a show the confirmed delete.

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 409 `REMOVAL_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED` with property `impact` (`dataSinks`, `layers`, `apis`, `requiresConfirmation`) if the confirmation is missing or incomplete.

  **Verification:** Issue TC-PIPE-02 for same `pipelineId` and confirm 404.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Pipeline record removed; DataSinks without a Pipeline deleted or marked `PENDING_UNPROVISION`, with their Layers and the APIs they alone backed |
  | Config Adapter | -- (the next release removes the storage of `PENDING_UNPROVISION` DataSinks) |
  | External System | -- |
}
